01:09:36.269 --> 01:09:40.584
Before we kick into anything else, we did have a closed

01:09:40.600 --> 01:09:42.685
meeting of council about an hour ago.

01:09:43.728 --> 01:09:47.370
And as I always do, I do a little bit of a, just very high-level

01:09:47.870 --> 01:09:51.525
summary. So we did go into closed session about an hour ago.

01:09:52.070 --> 01:09:55.615
It was only under one item titled, as on the

01:09:56.115 --> 01:10:00.171
open agenda, Comprehensive Zoning Bylaw Appeals Ontario Land

01:10:00.671 --> 01:10:04.084
Tribunal Update. And my high-level summary there is

01:10:04.678 --> 01:10:08.445
that we had a discussion on that matter with legal and we

01:10:08.945 --> 01:10:11.971
gave direction. So council gave direction on that matter to legal.

01:10:12.212 --> 01:10:16.139
Okay. So that's it for the summary on that.

01:10:17.005 --> 01:10:20.387
And so with that, please stand if you are able as we

01:10:20.887 --> 01:10:22.872
recognize our national anthem.

01:11:50.738 --> 01:11:54.415
Great, thank you so much everyone. Just a moment of silent reflection

01:11:54.511 --> 01:11:55.185
as we continue.

01:12:06.383 --> 01:12:09.446
Thank you. And also for our Indigenous territorial acknowledgment.

01:12:10.409 --> 01:12:13.440
As we gather, let us take time to reflect on our privilege to live and

01:12:13.940 --> 01:12:17.305
work here in Guelph, a city built over rich Indigenous histories. And as guests

01:12:17.805 --> 01:12:21.538
here, we should reflect upon the responsibility to care for this land and

01:12:21.554 --> 01:12:24.521
the people who live here today and the generations to come.

01:12:24.826 --> 01:12:28.739
And if our actions today can move us towards reconciliation, we should take pause

01:12:29.253 --> 01:12:31.546
and make those decisions with intention and gratitude.

01:12:32.524 --> 01:12:35.925
This place we call Guelph has served as traditional lands and a place of refuge

01:12:36.053 --> 01:12:39.581
for many peoples over time, but more specifically, the Anishnaabeg Mi'kmaq First Nation

01:12:40.081 --> 01:12:43.976
and the Haudenosaunee. This land is held as the treaty lands and territory

01:12:44.072 --> 01:12:47.745
with the Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation, and Guelph lies directly adjacent

01:12:48.018 --> 01:12:51.867
to the Haldimand Tract, which is part of a long-established traditional hunting grounds

01:12:52.011 --> 01:12:55.423
for the Six Nations of the Grand River. Many First Nations,

01:12:55.456 --> 01:12:59.650
Inuit, and Métis people who have come from across Turtle Island call Guelph

01:13:00.150 --> 01:13:00.152
home today.

01:13:04.100 --> 01:13:07.609
All right, any disclosure of pecuniary interest or any general nature

01:13:07.754 --> 01:13:11.570
thereof for any of the items in front of us today? I have

01:13:11.698 --> 01:13:14.355
