01:13:18.524 --> 01:13:22.081
Uh, yes, Mr. Mayor, um, 6.2 related to the College Avenue

01:13:22.581 --> 01:13:23.755
development. It is directly adjacent and will impact my employer.

01:13:26.294 --> 01:13:29.971
All right, thank you. And Councillor Hauser, over to

01:13:29.987 --> 01:13:32.717
you. Am I going to hear the word ditto? You can hear ditto.

01:13:33.375 --> 01:13:36.715
Okay, so the same, the same issue. And I know that both of

01:13:37.215 --> 01:13:40.424
you disclosed it to us, now doing it publicly, and you've

01:13:40.924 --> 01:13:44.005
filled out the form that will be needed. And so we thank you for doing

01:13:44.037 --> 01:13:47.586
that. So when we get to that item, um, you know, both of you should

01:13:47.650 --> 01:13:51.525
probably just make sure that you leave the council chambers Make

01:13:52.025 --> 01:13:54.646
sure that you turn off your camera and just don't interact at all, and then

01:13:54.840 --> 01:13:56.635
when it's done, we'll make sure we invite you back in.

01:13:58.550 --> 01:14:01.839
Okay, so since

01:14:02.339 --> 01:14:03.987
it's my last two meetings here,

01:14:04.988 --> 01:14:08.671
I'm taking the liberty to have a little bit of fun at the beginning

01:14:08.784 --> 01:14:12.075
and at the end of the meeting. I found

01:14:12.575 --> 01:14:16.617
this book on my desk when I came in to

01:14:17.117 --> 01:14:21.316
City Hall. Someone has written a book called Guelph Trivia:

01:14:21.477 --> 01:14:25.253
The Bicentennial, and it's a trivia book for the 200th

01:14:25.431 --> 01:14:28.965
birthday coming up. So just a little

01:14:29.047 --> 01:14:31.225
bit of audience interaction.

01:14:32.152 --> 01:14:38.315
Someone yell out a number between 1 and 420.

01:14:38.380 --> 01:14:40.704
1827. No.

01:14:41.753 --> 01:14:44.558
Someone yell out a number between 1 and 420.

01:14:50.146 --> 01:14:51.954
263. Let's see, everyone.

01:14:54.657 --> 01:14:58.730
All right, here's the question. Who has a TV

01:14:58.859 --> 01:15:02.339
bingo in Guelph? A, the Lions Club,

01:15:02.581 --> 01:15:06.339
B, the Rotary Club, C, the Kiwanis Club, or D, the Legion?

01:15:07.747 --> 01:15:10.596
Does anybody think they know what that answer is?

01:15:12.544 --> 01:15:14.029
Okay, Linda, do you know?

01:15:16.604 --> 01:15:19.157
It is the Lions Club. You are the winner.

01:15:21.224 --> 01:15:24.843
At the time, Rogers TV longstanding tradition of supporting local

01:15:25.343 --> 01:15:28.946
Lions Club and charities will continue with the TV bingo Wednesdays

01:15:29.301 --> 01:15:33.189
at 8 PM. So that's pretty cool. So I don't know,

01:15:33.721 --> 01:15:37.061
Michael Noonan, Michael Noonan is the author of

01:15:37.125 --> 01:15:40.295
this Guelph Trivia Bicentennial, and there's like 400 questions.

01:15:40.902 --> 01:15:43.921
And it's pretty cool. We'll do another one at the end of the council meeting,

01:15:43.937 --> 01:15:48.095
so stay tuned. All right? But Michael Noonan,

01:15:48.224 --> 01:15:51.965
thank you very much. And maybe all of you can maybe go check out this

01:15:52.465 --> 01:15:55.706
little local gem that was just done. I found it to be kind of fun.

01:15:56.461 --> 01:16:00.170
Okay, we've broken the ice, because we got a lot of

01:16:00.670 --> 01:16:03.622
agenda items in front of us today. We're kicking off, though,

01:16:04.007 --> 01:16:07.509
with the consent agenda. And as

01:16:07.621 --> 01:16:10.947
usual, I will yell out the titles, and if anyone wants them

01:16:10.996 --> 01:16:14.450
pulled, let me know. But the first one is 35 McTagg

01:16:14.466 --> 01:16:16.796
Street, which is the notice of intention to designate.

01:16:18.066 --> 01:16:21.280
Next is 41 Norwich Street East with the notice of intention to

01:16:21.780 --> 01:16:25.650
designate. Now, that was withdrawn as requested by the agent on behalf of

01:16:26.150 --> 01:16:29.314
the owner. 55 Baker Street, including 152 and

01:16:29.814 --> 01:16:33.379
160 Wyndham Street North, the heritage permit. And the

01:16:33.444 --> 01:16:36.819
designation of the Ward Heritage Conservation District.

01:16:38.208 --> 01:16:42.278
And that is it. So again, the 431 Norwich is not

01:16:42.409 --> 01:16:45.730
in it, but the rest are. Is there anyone that

01:16:46.230 --> 01:16:49.500
needs anything pulled? No? Would anyone be willing

01:16:49.598 --> 01:16:53.723
to move consent? Councilor Caron and Councilor

01:16:53.739 --> 01:16:56.815
Hauser, looks like you want to second that. Am I right?

01:16:56.960 --> 01:16:59.065
Yep, okay. Anything further?

01:17:00.297 --> 01:17:03.084
I'll call the vote. Is anyone against the consent items?

01:17:04.974 --> 01:17:06.242
Nobody. That's unanimous.

01:17:07.395 --> 01:17:10.872
Can I just say to the staff on the

01:17:10.888 --> 01:17:11.945
heritage district,

01:17:14.000 --> 01:17:17.056
well done. I don't know, I don't have my glasses on. Are you

01:17:17.104 --> 01:17:20.690
in the room? Thank you.

01:17:21.643 --> 01:17:26.095
Good job. And amazing

01:17:26.127 --> 01:17:29.814
engagement the whole way through, including the last time with draft

01:17:30.314 --> 01:17:33.021
and listening and some really good job. So well done.

01:17:34.144 --> 01:17:37.158
Okay, we got items for discussion. We got several.

01:17:38.457 --> 01:17:42.145
And I would submit that one of the big ones is the first

01:17:42.645 --> 01:17:45.688
one out of the gate that we're all ready for. And that is the decision

01:17:46.188 --> 01:17:49.793
report for 266 to 280 Clare Road West, 950 Southgate Drive.

01:17:49.841 --> 01:17:53.242
It's the OPA and ZBA file. We're going to hear

01:17:53.482 --> 01:17:57.031
from our own staff first, I think. Yep, you're here.

01:17:57.962 --> 01:18:00.997
Anad is here, and then we have 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6,

01:18:01.238 --> 01:18:04.594
7, 8. We've got 11 delegations.

01:18:05.894 --> 01:18:09.684
And just remember, all you 11 delegations, you got no more than 5 minutes.

01:18:10.486 --> 01:18:12.510
Okay? So please,

01:18:13.682 --> 01:18:17.070
over to our staff to kick us off with the presentation, okay?

01:18:24.603 --> 01:18:28.024
Good evening, Mayor and members of council. Uh, my name is Anand Shah.

01:18:28.168 --> 01:18:30.289
I'm senior planner with Planning and Building Services.

01:18:31.108 --> 01:18:34.786
Today, I, along with Krista Wauke, general manager of Planning and Building

01:18:34.818 --> 01:18:38.159
Services, will be presenting staff's review and recommendation

01:18:38.737 --> 01:18:43.186
regarding the official plan amendment and zoning bylaw amendment application for 266

01:18:43.251 --> 01:18:46.365
in 280 Clare Road West, and 950 Southgate Drive.

01:18:47.286 --> 01:18:51.128
The presentation will summarize the proposal, the requested planning approvals,

01:18:51.548 --> 01:18:55.284
key findings from staff's review, and staff's recommendation for council's

01:18:55.784 --> 01:18:55.980
consideration.

01:19:00.640 --> 01:19:04.007
The subject lands are municipally known as 266 Clare Road West,

01:19:04.281 --> 01:19:08.181
280 Clare Road West, and includes a portion of 950

01:19:08.681 --> 01:19:12.105
Southgate Drive. The properties are located in the south end of the

01:19:12.605 --> 01:19:15.779
city and includes both lands proposed for the development and

01:19:15.812 --> 01:19:19.685
lands associated with the proposed ecological linkage realignment.

01:19:23.730 --> 01:19:27.025
The applicant— the applicant proposes a residential development consisting

01:19:27.121 --> 01:19:30.754
of one 16-story apartment building, one 14-story apartment

01:19:31.254 --> 01:19:34.793
building, 15 blocks of back-to-back townhouses, 16 blocks

01:19:34.857 --> 01:19:38.528
of stacked townhouses for a total number of 940 dwelling

01:19:38.544 --> 01:19:42.609
units. The proposal also includes 1,077

01:19:42.705 --> 01:19:46.126
parking spaces through a combination of surface and covered parking.

01:19:47.267 --> 01:19:51.025
Access is proposed from Clare Road West, and the development also

01:19:51.057 --> 01:19:54.896
proposes to relocate, uh, the existing ecological linkage to

01:19:55.396 --> 01:19:59.232
the west property boundary with a reduction of width from 100m existing

01:19:59.409 --> 01:20:00.790
to 60m proposed.

01:20:06.299 --> 01:20:09.444
The slide— this slide illustrates the proposed site layout.

01:20:10.006 --> 01:20:13.537
The high-density apartment buildings comprising of approximately

01:20:14.037 --> 01:20:18.111
68% of the units of the total proposed are

01:20:18.611 --> 01:20:22.043
generally located towards the center and rear of the site, with townhouse

01:20:22.543 --> 01:20:26.456
blocks distributed throughout the development. A 6-story parking garage

01:20:26.472 --> 01:20:30.741
is also proposed at the rear end of the site, adjacent to the future ecological

01:20:30.774 --> 01:20:31.111
linkage.

01:20:36.701 --> 01:20:40.571
The applicant is requesting amendment to the official plan to redesignate the current

01:20:41.071 --> 01:20:44.808
employment, employment and natural heritage area and natural area

01:20:45.308 --> 01:20:49.375
designated lands to a high-density residential and natural heritage area

01:20:49.391 --> 01:20:52.910
and natural areas, along with site-specific policies.

01:20:54.574 --> 01:20:58.406
The site-specific policies requests including

01:20:59.323 --> 01:21:03.391
provision for townhouse forms within the high-density residential designation,

01:21:03.889 --> 01:21:07.428
building height up to 16 stories, residential densities

01:21:07.525 --> 01:21:10.912
up to 160 units per hectare, and a Class 4 noise

01:21:10.945 --> 01:21:12.926
designation under NPC 300.

01:21:17.602 --> 01:21:21.885
The application is requesting rezoning of the lands into a site-specific high-density

01:21:21.901 --> 01:21:25.673
residential RHC 7-26, along with holding provisions

01:21:25.850 --> 01:21:29.471
H-29 and NHS, to facilitate the proposed

01:21:29.971 --> 01:21:32.803
residential development and ecological linkage realignment.

01:21:33.557 --> 01:21:36.729
The application seeks a number of site-specific exceptions,

01:21:37.066 --> 01:21:40.847
including permitting back-to-back cluster stacked

01:21:40.911 --> 01:21:44.020
and stacked back-to-back townhouses into an RH-7 zone,

01:21:44.372 --> 01:21:47.817
permitting a maximum density of 154 units per hectare,

01:21:48.362 --> 01:21:57.942
increased building height of up to 16 stories Removal

01:21:57.990 --> 01:22:01.346
of floor plate area maximums, no step-back regulations

01:22:01.458 --> 01:22:04.975
for high-rise residential building, and reduce common amenity area and

01:22:05.055 --> 01:22:08.604
reduce parking requirements. The application is also

01:22:09.104 --> 01:22:12.859
proposing holding provisions related to exchange of ecological linkage lands

01:22:12.939 --> 01:22:14.625
and affordable housing commitment.

01:22:19.664 --> 01:22:23.210
After reviewing the applications against provincial and city policy frameworks,

01:22:23.387 --> 01:22:25.826
staff identified several significant concerns.

01:22:26.484 --> 01:22:30.639
First, the proposed conversion of employment land has not been justified

01:22:30.736 --> 01:22:34.490
as required by provincial planning statement policies and the city's official

01:22:34.506 --> 01:22:38.117
plan. Second, the staff cannot confirm that the proposed

01:22:38.617 --> 01:22:42.272
residential use will avoid adverse impact on future industrial operations

01:22:42.529 --> 01:22:46.476
in the surrounding industrial lands. The proposed ecological linkage

01:22:46.492 --> 01:22:50.150
relocation and design has not demonstrated to the staff

01:22:50.650 --> 01:22:54.257
satisfaction that ecological function and connectivity will be maintained or

01:22:54.757 --> 01:22:58.412
enhanced. Finally, concerns remains regarding the proposed placement

01:22:58.912 --> 01:23:02.086
of private stormwater management infrastructure within lands intended

01:23:02.118 --> 01:23:04.814
to become public ecological linkage lands.

01:23:05.728 --> 01:23:09.258
In the report, staff have identified potential issues

01:23:09.758 --> 01:23:13.718
regarding ownership, maintenance, operations, and liabilities associated with this approach.

01:23:14.472 --> 01:23:17.770
Additional concerns and details are outlined in the staff's, uh,

01:23:17.931 --> 01:23:21.888
report attachment 8, and all additional technical comments are provided

01:23:22.388 --> 01:23:22.803
in attachment 9.

01:23:26.932 --> 01:23:30.290
The proposed official plan and zoning bylaw amendment application do

01:23:30.790 --> 01:23:33.959
not currently conform with the Provincial Planning Statement 2024

01:23:34.313 --> 01:23:37.678
or the city's official plan and other applicable planning and engineering

01:23:37.726 --> 01:23:41.662
requirements. As a result, city staff are unable to recommend that

01:23:42.162 --> 01:23:45.961
council approve the application. And with that, I'll request Krista

01:23:46.461 --> 01:23:48.579
to come up here and continue the presentation. Thank you.

01:23:54.417 --> 01:23:57.815
All right, thank you, Anand. So we do

01:23:57.879 --> 01:24:01.180
recognize that this is a difficult decision for

01:24:01.680 --> 01:24:05.277
council. Staff are standing

01:24:05.777 --> 01:24:09.439
behind the recommendation that this is not a supported employment lands conversion.

01:24:10.139 --> 01:24:13.373
But we do understand the issue in front of council. So we have an

01:24:13.873 --> 01:24:17.107
alternative that we've presented in attachment 5 and 6 of the staff

01:24:17.607 --> 01:24:21.837
report. So I'm just going to walk council through that to understand why staff

01:24:21.869 --> 01:24:24.899
came up with this alternative recommendation and what it considers.

01:24:28.271 --> 01:24:32.040
So if council does want to amend the official

01:24:32.540 --> 01:24:35.760
plan from employment with the provision that

01:24:36.260 --> 01:24:40.390
we're going to be getting some affordable housing, staff have laid out the requirements,

01:24:40.873 --> 01:24:43.080
and obviously amending the land use designation,

01:24:43.998 --> 01:24:47.412
um, from employment to high-density residential is what

01:24:47.912 --> 01:24:51.148
we've shown on the map. From what, uh, Mr. Shaw presented,

01:24:51.422 --> 01:24:54.062
we've just evened out the map a little bit. There was a little bit of

01:24:54.562 --> 01:24:58.026
a hole in the donut, so we've, uh, for the NHS system, so we've just

01:24:58.526 --> 01:24:58.974
tidied it up a little bit.

01:25:02.559 --> 01:25:06.543
And then for the official plan alternative recommendations.

01:25:06.608 --> 01:25:10.470
We've kept many of the requests that have been submitted by the applicant,

01:25:10.486 --> 01:25:12.958
such as the density at 154 units.

01:25:14.724 --> 01:25:17.866
But that is, that is kind of what we have kept.

01:25:18.832 --> 01:25:23.586
We have a policy about 33% affordable

01:25:24.086 --> 01:25:27.550
housing. You're going to ask why 33%

01:25:27.955 --> 01:25:31.902
when at the public meeting the applicant presented there was going to be 50% affordable

01:25:32.402 --> 01:25:36.124
housing. The 33% of dwelling units

01:25:36.624 --> 01:25:40.277
that we're targeting to be affordable housing. So that's in keeping with our official plan

01:25:40.470 --> 01:25:43.869
and the housing affordability strategy that council approved earlier this term

01:25:44.318 --> 01:25:47.670
that recommends that 33% of all new units be affordable.

01:25:48.103 --> 01:25:51.983
So again, if we're converting employment land to housing,

01:25:52.336 --> 01:25:56.057
we are recommending that we meet the policy— policy 7.2

01:25:56.425 --> 01:25:58.991
of our official plan. So that is why we've recommended that.

01:26:00.018 --> 01:26:03.611
Um, we do note that since the public meeting, the applicant has

01:26:03.644 --> 01:26:07.718
requested that 10% of the units be affordable that meet

01:26:08.218 --> 01:26:11.906
our definition in the provincial bulletin. Um, staff are

01:26:12.406 --> 01:26:16.125
recommending 33%. That's what our affordable housing strategy recommends,

01:26:16.221 --> 01:26:20.456
and that's why we're asking for it in order that it be maintained

01:26:20.553 --> 01:26:22.895
as affordable. So the 33%,

01:26:23.938 --> 01:26:28.169
if it meets our definition We can secure it. There's recommendations

01:26:28.202 --> 01:26:31.908
in here for securing it and just to ensure that we meet that

01:26:32.408 --> 01:26:33.536
target that council's already approved.

01:26:40.584 --> 01:26:44.006
The applicant also requested 14,

01:26:44.504 --> 01:26:48.184
uh, 16 stories in height. Staff have recommended

01:26:48.216 --> 01:26:51.505
14. Why did we recommend 14? So this

01:26:51.937 --> 01:26:54.743
is a conversion from employment lands to high-density residential.

01:26:55.063 --> 01:26:58.686
High-density residential has a maximum height of 10 stories in our official

01:26:59.186 --> 01:27:02.501
plan. However, if you're in a strategic growth area such as along

01:27:02.598 --> 01:27:06.669
Gordon Street, um, we have up to 14 stories.

01:27:07.038 --> 01:27:10.981
So that is the maximum we have in strategic growth areas. This is neither,

01:27:11.591 --> 01:27:15.566
so that is why we could not support 16. But we are recommending

01:27:15.598 --> 01:27:19.034
that if council goes with the alternative that 14 is keeping with

01:27:19.534 --> 01:27:23.570
other sites earlier, earlier this year. For example, council approved

01:27:23.795 --> 01:27:26.871
the development at the, the Galaxy Cinema site, the one Clare wrote.

01:27:27.343 --> 01:27:30.775
That was at 14 stories, and that is in a strategic growth area.

01:27:34.908 --> 01:27:38.872
The density they requested, we have agreed to high

01:27:39.372 --> 01:27:44.851
density going to 154, and then there's a requirement

01:27:45.351 --> 01:27:46.688
that we've put in the official plan for noise guidelines. I'm going to get to

01:27:46.721 --> 01:27:47.883
that in a second.

01:27:51.132 --> 01:27:55.035
So in the site-specific zoning bylaw amendment, we have

01:27:55.164 --> 01:27:57.131
some alternative provisions.

01:27:59.400 --> 01:28:02.598
Um, they have asked for townhouse units

01:28:03.098 --> 01:28:05.796
to be on this site as well. We're supporting that back-to-back cluster stacked,

01:28:06.295 --> 01:28:10.712
whatever townhouse variation they choose, choose to build. So we've allowed For

01:28:11.212 --> 01:28:14.927
that, again, we're at the maximum height of 14

01:28:14.943 --> 01:28:17.843
stories. The density, uh,

01:28:18.629 --> 01:28:22.523
minimum common amenity area, they have asked for site-specific

01:28:22.555 --> 01:28:26.144
to 18.1

01:28:26.176 --> 01:28:29.221
meters per unit. We're supportive of that.

01:28:30.086 --> 01:28:34.301
And parking rate, we have said 1 space per unit plus 0.1

01:28:34.910 --> 01:28:38.116
visitor spaces. Per unit. So that's in keeping

01:28:38.165 --> 01:28:41.717
with our existing zoning for high-density residential sites generally.

01:28:46.980 --> 01:28:50.304
So Class 4 residential. This term

01:28:50.804 --> 01:28:54.419
of council has not approved a Class 4 residential

01:28:54.919 --> 01:28:59.416
use. A Class 4 residential use is defined

01:28:59.448 --> 01:29:03.205
under the Ministry of Environment, Conservation and Parks And it is— means

01:29:03.237 --> 01:29:06.463
it is a housing, a residential development, generally in built-up

01:29:06.527 --> 01:29:09.978
areas, so an infill development that has higher,

01:29:10.058 --> 01:29:13.557
higher noise volumes. So rather than

01:29:14.295 --> 01:29:17.617
45 decibels at night, you can have 55 decibels at night.

01:29:18.179 --> 01:29:21.806
So by— if council approves the change in, in land use for this,

01:29:22.817 --> 01:29:26.139
we are acknowledging based on their noise study that

01:29:26.284 --> 01:29:30.663
it is going to be potentially noisy here. So we

01:29:31.163 --> 01:29:33.341
also acknowledge that we're going to get complaints.

01:29:34.143 --> 01:29:37.671
So council, if they approve the zoning, is aware

01:29:37.912 --> 01:29:39.932
that we are supporting, um,

01:29:41.167 --> 01:29:44.840
higher noise from the adjacent industrial users

01:29:45.433 --> 01:29:49.490
on this site. So higher daytime noise, higher outside

01:29:50.004 --> 01:29:53.291
noise daytime and nighttime. So council has to be aware of that.

01:29:53.696 --> 01:29:57.017
You've not yet ever approved Class 4 residential during this term of

01:29:57.033 --> 01:29:57.375
council.

01:30:05.423 --> 01:30:09.405
Um, we do have some alternative recommendations

01:30:09.678 --> 01:30:13.342
in Attachment 6. So again, we talked about the affordable housing commit—

01:30:14.017 --> 01:30:17.752
commitment being 33%, that it be secured on title,

01:30:18.376 --> 01:30:21.957
and that so we ensure the long-term viability. Staff have recommended 49

01:30:22.327 --> 01:30:26.408
