02:45:26.529 --> 02:45:30.252
is putting in would push us down to 120 units

02:45:30.752 --> 02:45:34.443
per hectare. We need the larger floor plates to do the 154 per

02:45:34.943 --> 02:45:37.558
hectare. As long as we get the larger floor plates, it doesn't have to be

02:45:38.058 --> 02:45:41.620
14 floors— it doesn't have to be 16 floors. So it's just a function of

02:45:41.652 --> 02:45:45.024
having room for the volume volume that allows us to meet what staff has agreed

02:45:45.524 --> 02:45:49.472
to, which is 154 units per hectare. So, so that's— we've

02:45:49.520 --> 02:45:52.475
asked for it because it's simpler, but we don't have to have it.

02:45:53.053 --> 02:45:56.505
Okay, okay. And, and you would have the possibility of going, you know, like,

02:45:56.521 --> 02:45:59.556
like you have a bunch of townhouses, some of them could go up to 6

02:46:00.056 --> 02:46:03.425
stories, right, to make up the difference, as long as you maintain the density maximum

02:46:03.925 --> 02:46:08.210
of 154? Correct, except I am committed to family

02:46:08.710 --> 02:46:11.582
housing and families are better at grade than in an apartment building.

02:46:12.256 --> 02:46:15.355
So we could spread the density around as

02:46:15.452 --> 02:46:19.626
just apartment buildings, but if you've got 3 kids and can have an outside

02:46:20.126 --> 02:46:23.673
yard— so it's my desire to serve kids and families

02:46:23.721 --> 02:46:27.799
with kids so they have a choice. That means that we've made taller buildings

02:46:27.895 --> 02:46:31.219
to allow that to happen. Okay, okay, I appreciate that. Thank you.

02:46:31.508 --> 02:46:35.362
Thank you, Worship. Thank you. And Bucetot,

02:46:35.378 --> 02:46:38.493
please. Thank you. And through the mayor, thank you, Mr. LeVay.

02:46:38.991 --> 02:46:41.881
I'm just— I've been writing a whole bunch of notes. I just want to make

02:46:42.381 --> 02:46:46.280
sure my concluding statements are correct based on Mr. Handy's presentation and

02:46:46.361 --> 02:46:49.636
your delegation. What I have written down is you can live

02:46:49.749 --> 02:46:54.212
with the recommendations, the alternative recommendations,

02:46:54.260 --> 02:46:57.600
and the schedules that have been provided by staff. At the end of

02:46:58.100 --> 02:47:01.691
the day, and you know, to Council Mr. Downar's point. If we decide to go

02:47:01.707 --> 02:47:05.556
with the staff recommendations and that's the alternative

02:47:06.056 --> 02:47:10.302
recommendations that we provide to the staff, you're okay with that?

02:47:10.751 --> 02:47:14.038
To be clear, if you do not do any of the amendments we

02:47:14.538 --> 02:47:16.861
requested, we do not have a viable project.

02:47:17.903 --> 02:47:21.238
Now, I don't quit because you've told me once

02:47:21.816 --> 02:47:25.536
to try to build a non-viable project. We will be coming back

02:47:26.036 --> 02:47:29.388
to council after having discussed with staff, to ask for amendments.

02:47:29.453 --> 02:47:34.077
Because what staff has recommended in terms of the alternatives creates a non-viable

02:47:34.109 --> 02:47:37.320
project. It doesn't have the density required. It doesn't

02:47:37.820 --> 02:47:41.672
give us the affordability to serve kids. It doesn't do— it doesn't

02:47:41.720 --> 02:47:45.445
allow us to work with a proper size linkage.

02:47:46.296 --> 02:47:49.572
It shrinks the linkage and pushes it over so we have less ability to

02:47:49.604 --> 02:47:52.690
build the density that they've already agreed that we can build. No,

02:47:52.707 --> 02:47:56.221
if you're going to just say the alternative, it just— it's good

02:47:56.253 --> 02:47:59.638
because now we've changed the use. That's really good. But it's a

02:48:00.138 --> 02:48:03.125
non-viable project unless we have some of those amendments.

02:48:03.352 --> 02:48:07.571
Now, I've already said that some of them are flexible, but without

02:48:07.700 --> 02:48:10.885
giving us some of those amendments, you've just passed the decision

02:48:10.933 --> 02:48:14.451
on to the next council. Thank you.

02:48:17.958 --> 02:48:21.450
Okay, so the best part about

02:48:21.950 --> 02:48:26.373
being mayor is that you get to go last, and that's

02:48:26.873 --> 02:48:28.586
actually not true. I hate it every time I have to go last.

02:48:30.755 --> 02:48:38.217
So you

02:48:38.717 --> 02:48:42.294
said something about the city paying

02:48:42.668 --> 02:48:46.220
