03:10:55.827 --> 03:10:59.397
you know, comparing it to the noise that's coming from the road or from the

03:10:59.897 --> 03:11:02.668
Hanlon? What would the residents experience,

03:11:02.925 --> 03:11:06.929
and, you know, what level of noise would they actually be faced

03:11:06.961 --> 03:11:10.484
to? And this is— are you referring to the Hanlon? Specifically? Well,

03:11:10.998 --> 03:11:14.562
just give us a comparison that we can relate to so that when the residents

03:11:14.755 --> 03:11:18.994
are in that 14 or 16 story building and

03:11:19.331 --> 03:11:23.008
the manufacturing site is operating, what is the

03:11:23.024 --> 03:11:26.283
reality for them? I understand. So the criteria would be set, and then the Class

03:11:26.396 --> 03:11:30.153
4 designation is 55 decibels at night and 65 during

03:11:30.169 --> 03:11:33.284
the day. Between 55 and 60 decibels,

03:11:33.718 --> 03:11:36.977
again, for a comparison, is probably the sound level of a normal conversation.

03:11:37.796 --> 03:11:41.088
Okay, okay, so they're in their house, window closed, and there's

03:11:41.588 --> 03:11:45.005
that conversation happening outside of— outside the window. The criteria again

03:11:45.038 --> 03:11:47.976
is based on the outside of a window, not inside the unit.

03:11:48.233 --> 03:11:51.219
Transportation noise is a bit different, which is earlier in our report.

03:11:52.183 --> 03:11:54.800
That can be mitigated through increased thickness of windows,

03:11:55.876 --> 03:11:59.344
but the industrial noise is controlled on the outside

03:11:59.844 --> 03:12:02.202
of the window, so it needs to meet a the facade. Okay, okay, okay,

03:12:02.218 --> 03:12:04.980
I appreciate it. Because one of the main concerns that I heard back from my

03:12:05.831 --> 03:12:09.444
constituents after I asked this question, they said the quality of life of the people

03:12:09.944 --> 03:12:13.137
living there. But, but it sounds like with the mitigation, the quality of life would

03:12:13.637 --> 03:12:17.440
not be greatly diminished because of the proximity to the uses. And PDI is

03:12:17.472 --> 03:12:21.454
a little like rail shunting, is, is a significant

03:12:21.486 --> 03:12:25.067
noise source. That is, that is, PDI is a Class 3 industry under the D-Series

03:12:25.083 --> 03:12:28.323
guidelines, the ones in this area are Class 2. Okay, okay, I appreciate that.

03:12:28.485 --> 03:12:32.069
Thank you. Thank you. So the takeaway

03:12:32.117 --> 03:12:35.481
here, Councillor Goller, is don't have conversations outside people's windows.

03:12:36.067 --> 03:12:38.819
All right, all right, I think that's it.

03:12:39.649 --> 03:12:43.922
Thank you. All right, thank you very much. And Sal Spitali

03:12:44.131 --> 03:12:47.464
is coming up from North South Environmental,

03:12:47.560 --> 03:12:51.199
and then is Jay Hawkins here? Okay,

03:12:51.279 --> 03:12:54.528
you're in the wings. Okay. Over to you. Go right

03:12:55.028 --> 03:12:58.618
ahead. Thank you, Mr. Mayor, members of council. My name is Sal Spitali.

03:12:58.667 --> 03:13:01.912
I'm a senior ecologist with North South Environmental. I was

03:13:02.009 --> 03:13:05.603
retained to complete an environmental impact study for the subject lands.

03:13:09.200 --> 03:13:13.156
Um, and the environmental impact study was triggered due to the presence

03:13:13.366 --> 03:13:16.903
of an ecological linkage that was mapped in the city's official plan,

03:13:17.016 --> 03:13:21.065
as well as adjacent lands, which include significant

03:13:21.565 --> 03:13:24.628
landform. As part of the environmental impact study, we looked

03:13:25.128 --> 03:13:29.154
at the site and characterized it through a series of surveys

03:13:29.410 --> 03:13:32.123
and ecological inventories, breeding bird surveys,

03:13:32.299 --> 03:13:36.054
vegetation inventories, bat acoustic surveys,

03:13:37.210 --> 03:13:39.954
reptile emergence surveys, and a tree inventory.

03:13:41.078 --> 03:13:44.320
We also looked at the history of the subject lands to understand the vegetation

03:13:44.820 --> 03:13:48.192
vegetation characterization on site. Historically, back in the

03:13:48.692 --> 03:13:52.434
'50s, it was devoid of any vegetation. It was an agricultural land,

03:13:53.575 --> 03:13:57.544
primarily used for agricultural purposes. Some portions still are.

03:13:58.074 --> 03:14:02.220
Other areas have regenerated with natural vegetation

03:14:02.831 --> 03:14:06.350
with various concentrations or densities

03:14:06.850 --> 03:14:09.949
of trees, which go from cultural meadow, cultural thicket,

03:14:10.206 --> 03:14:13.565
Cultural Savannah. That's what differentiates some of the natural areas

03:14:13.741 --> 03:14:17.678
on site. Through our surveys, we didn't identify anything on the

03:14:18.178 --> 03:14:21.936
subject lands that would be additional significant natural

03:14:21.953 --> 03:14:25.375
features or areas, but of course, with the ecological linkage,

03:14:25.568 --> 03:14:28.814
we needed to consider the proposal that was before

03:14:28.926 --> 03:14:32.927
us to modify or look to move the ecological linkage.

03:14:33.843 --> 03:14:37.811
And with that, the development that was being proposed, the first thing that

03:14:37.923 --> 03:14:41.841
we provided was the constraint of the ecological linkage, looking at

03:14:41.873 --> 03:14:44.956
best practices and guidance documents for

03:14:45.068 --> 03:14:48.296
ecological linkages of this type and for the wildlife

03:14:48.796 --> 03:14:51.941
that would be expected to use it, typically deer,

03:14:52.551 --> 03:14:56.244
coyotes, foxes, small mammals that you would expect to find

03:14:56.725 --> 03:15:00.579
using this area. And based on those guidance

03:15:01.079 --> 03:15:04.220
documents, Natural Heritage Reference Manual, Environment Canada's How

03:15:04.720 --> 03:15:08.750
Much Habitat Is Enough, they recommend 50 to 100 meters for ecological

03:15:08.766 --> 03:15:12.234
linkage for generalist species. Again, those species that I had mentioned.

03:15:13.790 --> 03:15:17.126
And so we looked at that when we informed the

03:15:17.207 --> 03:15:20.946
recommendation for the linkage width, as well as the function

03:15:21.075 --> 03:15:24.345
of the linkage. We looked at the density of trees

03:15:24.845 --> 03:15:28.124
that are currently there and the current land use. With a mix of some

03:15:28.188 --> 03:15:32.276
natural areas and existing agricultural land use, and the density

03:15:32.776 --> 03:15:36.300
of trees being approximately 133 trees per hectare.

03:15:37.101 --> 03:15:40.372
And we're proposing the ecological linkage to be refined,

03:15:40.532 --> 03:15:43.786
reduced in width, as well as moved to the west portion of

03:15:43.818 --> 03:15:47.762
the subject lands, and that it would be planted with a much higher density

03:15:48.262 --> 03:15:51.850
of trees with some other habitat elements included in it. So it would,

03:15:52.315 --> 03:15:56.045
in effect, have a higher function and a higher ability

03:15:56.545 --> 03:16:00.184
for wildlife to use the ecological linkage than in its current form or

03:16:00.313 --> 03:16:04.364
location as it traverses the land. So the intent

03:16:04.509 --> 03:16:08.116
and the purpose of our recommendations for the restoration of the linkage,

03:16:08.309 --> 03:16:11.792
even with the reduction to 60 meters, would be to improve

03:16:12.292 --> 03:16:15.931
and increase its function and use by wildlife. Um,

03:16:16.144 --> 03:16:19.902
and of course, the— this is all being couched within because consideration

03:16:19.998 --> 03:16:24.077
of the policies to ensure that the opportunity

03:16:24.173 --> 03:16:27.690
to refine the linkage, reduce the width, conformed with the policies

03:16:27.722 --> 03:16:31.511
in the official plan, as well as ensuring that

03:16:31.655 --> 03:16:35.686
the intent of maintaining or enhancing the function was

03:16:36.186 --> 03:16:39.587
achieved. So that's how our design was proposed, and that's, that's what we were

03:16:40.087 --> 03:16:43.859
intending to do here. We also considered the stormwater management

03:16:43.875 --> 03:16:47.519
design. Where stormwater would be directed to a portion of

03:16:47.535 --> 03:16:50.907
the ecological linkage, which is technically permitted under the

03:16:51.407 --> 03:16:54.825
policies of the official plan, where a portion of your ecological linkage can

03:16:54.857 --> 03:16:58.261
serve as stormwater management. And in this case,

03:16:58.390 --> 03:17:02.645
we ensured that how it would be designed, the water that would be

03:17:03.145 --> 03:17:06.819
directed there, the duration of the— any sort of flooding in the area, and the

03:17:06.884 --> 03:17:10.352
vegetation that we were proposing in the ecological linkage would be

03:17:10.852 --> 03:17:14.639
able to sustain any sort of infrequent

03:17:15.554 --> 03:17:19.391
flooding events that occur from water being directed into

03:17:19.424 --> 03:17:22.972
the Ecological Linkage. So all of those design considerations

03:17:23.020 --> 03:17:27.195
for the Ecological Linkage factored in, including the stormwater

03:17:27.695 --> 03:17:31.353
management. So based on the findings of the EIS and with consideration

03:17:31.369 --> 03:17:34.677
of those policies, it was our opinion that we would be

03:17:35.177 --> 03:17:39.238
able to, through the relocation and enhancement and restoration

03:17:39.431 --> 03:17:43.192
of the ecological linkage maintain the function,

03:17:43.773 --> 03:17:46.988
uh, and by meeting those policies. Thank you.

03:17:49.348 --> 03:17:52.645
Thank you. Um, any questions

03:17:52.823 --> 03:17:56.397
on this conversation? Okay, uh, Councillor Alt,

03:17:56.462 --> 03:17:59.617
please. I got 3. It's a quick one, and thank you for the

03:18:00.117 --> 03:18:03.452
presentation. Uh, in looking at the linkage, I just realized

03:18:03.952 --> 03:18:07.564
it is now much closer, almost exactly on the curvature of

03:18:08.064 --> 03:18:11.525
the road. Does that cause any challenge to

03:18:11.896 --> 03:18:14.851
any wildlife that might be crossing at that point?

03:18:17.010 --> 03:18:18.464
Thank you, Mr. Mayor. Thank you for the question.

