04:53:49.141 --> 04:53:52.361
Thank you, Mr. Mayor, councillors,

04:53:52.703 --> 04:53:55.848
ladies and gentlemen. My wife and I

04:53:56.348 --> 04:53:59.802
live at 204 College Avenue East, and we border

04:53:59.882 --> 04:54:02.952
the proposed development immediately to the west.

04:54:04.589 --> 04:54:08.307
Excuse me. I purchased the property

04:54:08.340 --> 04:54:12.776
at 204 College Avenue East in 1973 while

04:54:13.276 --> 04:54:15.282
a postgraduate student at the University of Waterloo.

04:54:17.265 --> 04:54:20.454
My parents lived in the house for 23 happy years.

04:54:21.452 --> 04:54:25.800
My wife and I are both retired and plan to enjoy this

04:54:26.300 --> 04:54:30.035
home in our retirement. We have recently built

04:54:30.535 --> 04:54:36.536
a new top story on our house as well as a small garage/house

04:54:37.312 --> 04:54:41.218
on the back lot of the property. We are the

04:54:41.718 --> 04:54:44.632
only house that is not bought and being demolished.

04:54:47.035 --> 04:54:50.678
We're not against student housing. When I bought the house

04:54:50.823 --> 04:54:54.769
in 1973, I rented out to students for many years, and some

04:54:54.801 --> 04:54:57.130
of these students became lifelong friends.

04:55:01.108 --> 04:55:04.852
Since the first contact with the developers and the city planning

04:55:04.884 --> 04:55:08.224
department, the development proposal has changed

04:55:09.327 --> 04:55:13.904
Initially, it was for a 10-story student house accommodating

04:55:14.357 --> 04:55:17.866
434 beds, then an 8-story building,

04:55:18.319 --> 04:55:22.056
and now it's a 7-story, 171-unit apartment building.

04:55:22.185 --> 04:55:26.452
Initially, the entrance

04:55:26.613 --> 04:55:29.933
to the underground garage was at the east end of development.

04:55:30.161 --> 04:55:33.221
Now it is the west end next to our driveway.

04:55:34.441 --> 04:55:38.351
Since there are not enough above-ground parking

04:55:39.530 --> 04:55:43.359
for pizza deliveries, Ubers, drop-offs, etc., there will

04:55:43.375 --> 04:55:47.352
be a congestion at the entrance to the proposed development, and this will pose a

04:55:47.416 --> 04:55:50.894
traffic hazard only exacerbated by the fact that

04:55:50.942 --> 04:55:54.278
the driveway is at the crest of a hill and

04:55:54.778 --> 04:55:58.278
there are blind spots. I would like to ask

04:55:58.778 --> 04:56:01.987
council, through the mayor, to refer the report back to staff

04:56:02.534 --> 04:56:05.056
reporting in the first quarter of 2027.

04:56:09.082 --> 04:56:12.707
I would like to put a direct question through the mayor to

04:56:13.207 --> 04:56:15.927
the applicant if the applicant consents to such a referral.

04:56:18.579 --> 04:56:22.137
I would like to remind the applicant that their own solicitor wrote

04:56:22.637 --> 04:56:26.419
to the city in May asking for a deferral so that they could work

04:56:26.919 --> 04:56:27.835
through staff comments.

04:56:30.575 --> 04:56:34.768
The applicant reviewed such a def— uh, received such a deferral,

04:56:35.367 --> 04:56:37.197
and I'm asking the same courtesy.

04:56:42.556 --> 04:56:46.098
I'm not asking council to outright refuse the application. However,

04:56:46.903 --> 04:56:49.141
if council will not, uh, approve the,

04:56:50.027 --> 04:56:53.847
uh, application, then I ask that council insist to

04:56:53.863 --> 04:56:54.901
include every, uh,

04:56:57.373 --> 04:57:00.576
protection the staff recommended without relinquishing

04:57:00.689 --> 04:57:00.900
any.

04:57:05.337 --> 04:57:09.100
The zoning of our property, as well as the zoning of the 3

04:57:09.600 --> 04:57:14.289
properties that are slated for development, are presently zoned

04:57:14.789 --> 04:57:18.137
density— low density RL-1. This allows

04:57:18.234 --> 04:57:21.600
for the construction of dwellings up to a maximum height of 3 stories

04:57:22.429 --> 04:57:26.190
and we would welcome such a development. However, the proposed rezoning,

04:57:26.945 --> 04:57:30.851
uh, of the 3 neighboring lots is for high-density residential

04:57:31.191 --> 04:57:34.870
with a 7-story apartment building containing 117 dwelling units

04:57:34.919 --> 04:57:37.549
and 69 underground parking spaces.

04:57:38.775 --> 04:57:42.867
The footprint of this building is 151 feet by 158

04:57:43.367 --> 04:57:46.818
feet, and there are minimal setbacks.

04:57:48.357 --> 04:57:51.482
To get an idea of what the size of this

04:57:51.694 --> 04:57:54.974
building will be, you can take an American football field,

04:57:55.006 --> 04:57:58.336
which is 160 feet wide, and you form a

04:57:58.836 --> 04:58:02.295
square, 160 feet on each side,

04:58:02.655 --> 04:58:03.768
and you go up 7 stories.

04:58:06.260 --> 04:58:09.499
Section 1 of the staff report states that the proposed

04:58:09.612 --> 04:58:13.780
building has no unacceptable adverse impact on

04:58:13.878 --> 04:58:17.174
adjacent building, including our

04:58:17.223 --> 04:58:19.545
home. We certainly do not agree with this.

04:58:26.997 --> 04:58:30.659
I think that was a bell. You have 30 more seconds.

04:58:30.951 --> 04:58:36.567
30 seconds? Yeah. Okay. Well, I think that is attached—

04:58:37.424 --> 04:58:41.247
the document is attached to the agenda and it

04:58:41.747 --> 04:58:46.956
gives some issues that I think consider—

04:58:47.828 --> 04:58:51.738
should be considered, such as— okay,

04:58:52.093 --> 04:58:55.709
thank you. No, no problem. Thank you very much

04:58:56.209 --> 04:58:58.008
for your delegation. Don't go away yet just in case there's a question.

04:58:59.891 --> 04:59:03.518
Okay, I have a question for you. Yes. Not wanting you to like have to

04:59:03.567 --> 04:59:07.377
continue with your delegation, I was already thinking about asking this 2

04:59:07.393 --> 04:59:11.689
minutes ago. So are there like site-specific

04:59:11.867 --> 04:59:16.051
issues that you're looking for other

04:59:16.551 --> 04:59:19.702
than just not a— such

04:59:20.202 --> 04:59:24.292
a tall building going to like a 3-story building? Is there something else

04:59:24.792 --> 04:59:28.141
that you were looking for, like something that you

04:59:29.935 --> 04:59:33.003
could leave with us? Or I just want to— No,

04:59:33.035 --> 04:59:36.455
it's really the size of the development. I mean, we will be

04:59:36.955 --> 04:59:39.233
living in a canyon and on display.

04:59:40.550 --> 04:59:43.793
It is overwhelming. The building is just overwhelming. Okay.

04:59:44.580 --> 04:59:48.498
Okay. And have you had any conversations with the developer at

04:59:48.998 --> 04:59:52.367
all in regards to being the neighbor to this? Well,

04:59:52.431 --> 04:59:55.707
yes. Initially, we were— we kept an

04:59:55.819 --> 04:59:59.418
open mind. But we finally decided that we really would not

04:59:59.918 --> 05:00:03.596
like to live beside such a development. And so we expressed the fact that we

05:00:04.096 --> 05:00:06.344
were very much against it. Okay. Okay.

05:00:07.372 --> 05:00:11.501
All right. I appreciate that clarity. And, and thank you very much for

05:00:11.566 --> 05:00:14.715
your delegation for waiting around to do that. So, okay, no problem. Thank you.

05:00:14.940 --> 05:00:18.925
Thank you. Okay. We have Rachel Bozzi

05:00:18.957 --> 05:00:24.788
from GSP Group is here and Juliane

05:00:24.900 --> 05:00:28.304
von Westerholt is maybe— are you here?

05:00:29.075 --> 05:00:30.922
Okay, you're in the wings, okay.

05:00:32.142 --> 05:00:35.305
So Rachel, go right ahead.

05:00:36.060 --> 05:00:38.966
That's my wife's name. It's a good name. You told me that before.

05:00:39.030 --> 05:00:42.001
Yeah. Okay, I'm good to start?

05:00:42.482 --> 05:00:45.694
Yep. Okay, through the mayor, good evening. My name is Rachel Bossie,

05:00:45.774 --> 05:00:49.003
and I'm a senior planner with GSP Group. Uh, joining us

05:00:49.503 --> 05:00:52.674
in person tonight are the applicant Elysium and the urban designer who will be

05:00:52.756 --> 05:00:53.566
available for Q&amp;A.

05:00:58.583 --> 05:01:02.197
So after the public meeting on April 15th, we worked

05:01:02.697 --> 05:01:06.007
with staff and met with the adjacent property owners in attempt to address the comments

05:01:06.039 --> 05:01:09.317
that were received. In reviewing the staff report, we're generally

05:01:09.349 --> 05:01:13.117
supportive and we're thankful for staff for their hard work over the past 9 months.

05:01:13.872 --> 05:01:17.959
We would like to highlight 4 items from the staff recommendation. So the first

05:01:18.459 --> 05:01:21.724
being building height, 8 stories was proposed. The shadow study and the staff

05:01:22.224 --> 05:01:26.308
analysis confirmed that at 8 stories, the development meets the city sun and shadow criteria

05:01:27.013 --> 05:01:30.747
for the surrounding lands, including the adjacent golf course and residential use.

05:01:31.323 --> 05:01:34.849
In addition, 8 stories result in a broader range of unit types,

05:01:34.865 --> 05:01:38.631
including 2, 3, 4-bedroom units, provides enhanced indoor

05:01:39.131 --> 05:01:42.803
amenities and improves the connection between outdoor and out— indoor and outdoor

05:01:43.303 --> 05:01:46.543
amenity areas on the ground floor. Uh, second being parking.

05:01:46.655 --> 05:01:50.074
A rate of 0.589 spaces per dwelling

05:01:50.122 --> 05:01:53.605
unit was proposed, including 10% visitor parking, and was

05:01:53.637 --> 05:01:57.441
supported by a parking study that reflects the site's walkable location,

05:01:57.553 --> 05:02:01.389
extensive bicycle parking supply, and the provision of a car share space.

05:02:02.288 --> 05:02:05.658
In our view, this strikes the appropriate balance between meeting and anticipated demand

05:02:06.158 --> 05:02:09.990
without providing excess parking. And then the third, pickup and drop-off, the site

05:02:10.490 --> 05:02:14.001
proposes one at-grade puto space, and the transportation engineer's analysis

05:02:14.501 --> 05:02:18.349
reviews function, queuing, time of day variations, and concluded that

05:02:18.734 --> 05:02:22.793
the pickup drop-off at grade is appropriate to accommodate the expected needs

05:02:22.841 --> 05:02:26.307
of the site. And then any operational adjustments can be made through site plan.

05:02:26.836 --> 05:02:30.221
And then finally, the previous three comments were

05:02:30.638 --> 05:02:34.516
notes that we wanted to clarify. But then what we are requesting is that

05:02:34.548 --> 05:02:38.186
the proposed holding provision be removed. So the matters included in

05:02:38.218 --> 05:02:41.551
the holding provision are already, already identified in Attachment

05:02:41.583 --> 05:02:45.253
4 as conditions of site plan approval, to which we have no objection.

05:02:45.782 --> 05:02:49.115
So keeping the holding provisions would duplicate the requirements that are

05:02:49.615 --> 05:02:52.801
already required through site plan and will and are always secured

05:02:53.301 --> 05:02:56.828
through site plan. So this further introduces a new approval step without

05:02:57.328 --> 05:03:01.224
providing any corresponding planning benefit. So we respectfully

05:03:01.241 --> 05:03:04.558
ask that council approve the staff recommendation as set out in the decision but

05:03:05.058 --> 05:03:05.794
without the holding provisions.

05:03:10.964 --> 05:03:14.492
So after the public meeting in April, the proposal was revised to address the

05:03:14.992 --> 05:03:18.455
comments received and the June 17th resubmission included a reduction to the

05:03:18.955 --> 05:03:22.023
number of units by 36, the height by 2 stories and

05:03:22.523 --> 05:03:25.651
increase the parking rate by an additional 0.16 spaces per unit.

05:03:29.980 --> 05:03:33.273
So the next 3 slides illustrate changes made to the proposal in response to

05:03:33.289 --> 05:03:36.551
the comment received, and this slide shows the revision to the building

05:03:36.599 --> 05:03:39.896
massing, including a reduction in the angular plane along the

05:03:40.396 --> 05:03:43.718
westerly lot line and an increased tower setback along the westerly lot

05:03:44.218 --> 05:03:46.115
line from 9.5m to 13.6m.

05:03:53.636 --> 05:03:57.145
The revised site plan includes 4 additional parking spaces,

05:03:57.257 --> 05:03:59.837
and including a dedicated car share space,

05:04:00.366 --> 05:04:04.468
along with several pickup and drop-off options. These included an at-grade

05:04:04.968 --> 05:04:08.490
puto space, which is a pickup drop-off, a loading bay that can accommodate

05:04:08.990 --> 05:04:13.105
up to 3 short-term spaces for scheduled use, a dedicated move-in

05:04:13.605 --> 05:04:17.543
and staging area. And at the same time, the bicycle parking supply has been maintained

05:04:18.043 --> 05:04:21.738
despite the reduction in the unit count, increasing the per-unit provision of

05:04:22.238 --> 05:04:25.796
long-term bicycle parking and further supporting active transportation and

05:04:25.812 --> 05:04:29.211
the use of the proposed multi-use trail on College Avenue.

05:04:34.626 --> 05:04:38.100
Oh, how do I go back? Is it this? Okay.

05:04:40.177 --> 05:04:44.056
So as requested at the public meeting, this 3D rendering illustrates the proposed

05:04:44.556 --> 05:04:48.162
development in relation to the existing grade along College Avenue East and

05:04:48.179 --> 05:04:50.382
demonstrates how it fits in with the surrounding context.

05:04:54.540 --> 05:04:58.436
So we appreciate staff and members of public input on the proposed development,

05:04:58.758 --> 05:05:02.058
and in closing, this development is good land use planning and it will benefit the

05:05:02.558 --> 05:05:06.185
greater community. And as indicated and by staff in the staff report,

05:05:06.265 --> 05:05:09.594
it's appropriate for the site. As such, we request that

05:05:10.094 --> 05:05:13.681
council approve the staff recommendation with the exception of the holding provisions. And as

05:05:13.730 --> 05:05:17.348
noted, both Elysium and the urban designer are here in person and will

05:05:17.848 --> 05:05:20.448
be happy to answer, and I also would be happy to answer any questions.

05:05:20.901 --> 05:05:24.003
Thank you so much for your time. Great, thank you

05:05:24.068 --> 05:05:27.726
very much. Appreciate it. Uh, any questions at this time?

05:05:29.936 --> 05:05:33.340
I have one. Do you have— oh, sorry, I see my council colleagues first.

05:05:33.709 --> 05:05:36.792
Councillor Bucettil, then I'll go to myself. Go ahead. Thank you.

05:05:36.840 --> 05:05:39.907
And through the mayor, I apologize. I thought when you took a breath you were

05:05:40.407 --> 05:05:43.986
finished, so I had put my hand up. Thank you for the presentation. I do

05:05:44.486 --> 05:05:48.112
have a question. I, and I asked this when you presented last

05:05:48.612 --> 05:05:52.142
time on this development, and it was around family housing.

05:05:52.592 --> 05:05:56.173
And I know that you're playing 2, 3, and 4-bedroom configurations.

05:05:56.767 --> 05:06:00.219
But yet in the— in some of the materials, I noticed still a reference

05:06:00.719 --> 05:06:04.378
and an assistance that this is a student residence. Can you comment

05:06:04.878 --> 05:06:08.247
on that? And then I have a further question. So, through Your Worship, the staff

05:06:08.747 --> 05:06:11.908
recommendation is referring this to as an apartment building, and we have no objection.

05:06:12.823 --> 05:06:16.645
Families could live in the units. There, there's plenty of 4 bedrooms

05:06:16.677 --> 05:06:20.065
that could accommodate students, although that hasn't been the target market.

05:06:20.113 --> 05:06:23.116
There would be nothing precluding families from living in the units.

05:06:24.820 --> 05:06:27.927
Thank you for that clarification. So a 4-bedroom would be configured

05:06:28.427 --> 05:06:30.922
not like a student residence with, you know, a central,

05:06:31.518 --> 05:06:35.227
you know, kitchenette and rooms off there, that a family could actually live

05:06:35.727 --> 05:06:36.815
there? If you can just clarify that.

05:06:38.872 --> 05:06:42.298
So through Your Worship, I'm getting the nod, uh, back there from,

05:06:42.635 --> 05:06:46.190
um, Elysium that yes, a family could live in, in those units,

05:06:46.206 --> 05:06:49.470
and there's there's the option of— there's 2, 3, and 4 bedrooms.

05:06:50.771 --> 05:06:53.725
Thank you. And I guess my hesitation is, you know, I think back to college,

05:06:53.837 --> 05:06:58.012
my colleague in Ward 5, College Avenue, where the developer

05:06:58.512 --> 05:07:01.689
was going to build seniors housing for seniors, and it

05:07:02.189 --> 05:07:05.607
ended up student housing. So, you know, from where we sit, this is

05:07:05.703 --> 05:07:08.417
a planning issue, and we're trying to look for a mix of housing.

05:07:09.075 --> 05:07:12.527
Um, can you speak again a little bit more about the holding provision,

05:07:12.543 --> 05:07:15.498
because I see no reason for removing that.

05:07:15.915 --> 05:07:19.608
Just understanding a little bit better. So through your worship, I can answer

05:07:20.108 --> 05:07:23.526
kind of a one-parter, but then Alicia might be able to provide some sort

05:07:24.026 --> 05:07:27.380
of additional implications of what that would mean kind of from their side. But from

05:07:27.396 --> 05:07:30.655
a planning perspective, there was two holding provisions, and Kelly,

05:07:30.752 --> 05:07:34.669
correct me if I'm wrong, one of them required an updated transportation study,

05:07:35.103 --> 05:07:39.406
and then the other required an updated stormwater management

05:07:39.906 --> 05:07:43.276
study. Those are things that were included in the attachment 4 as requirements

05:07:43.776 --> 05:07:47.370
for site plan approval that we will be doing anyway. So our

05:07:47.870 --> 05:07:50.999
experience typically would be that a hold would get you something extra that you wouldn't

05:07:51.499 --> 05:07:55.414
commonly get through site plan. And then if I could invite,

