05:10:35.324 --> 05:10:38.407
ID? No problem. So can

05:10:38.907 --> 05:10:41.626
you just state where you're from again? Yes, good evening. My name is Julianne von

05:10:41.658 --> 05:10:45.521
Westerholt. I'm a registered professional planner and a land use planning consultant

05:10:46.021 --> 05:10:49.386
at MHBC Planning, appearing today on behalf of my client,

05:10:49.467 --> 05:10:52.978
the Cotton Club, the owner and operator of the lands immediately

05:10:53.075 --> 05:10:57.182
to the north, east, and west of the proposed development that is

05:10:57.360 --> 05:11:01.478
under consideration this evening. Cotton Fields,

05:11:01.851 --> 05:11:06.687
my client, is not opposed to the redevelopment of the subject lands and

05:11:07.187 --> 05:11:10.829
to additional housing, nor are they opposed to purpose-built housing serving

05:11:10.861 --> 05:11:14.362
the university community. Since the initial meeting

05:11:14.378 --> 05:11:18.119
with council in April, and I attended that meeting, we have met with city staff

05:11:18.649 --> 05:11:21.989
and expressed the following specific concerns of our client as

05:11:22.101 --> 05:11:24.879
raised at the public meeting in April. These,

05:11:25.248 --> 05:11:28.508
these considerations include building height and massing, overlook,

05:11:29.070 --> 05:11:31.783
shadow and wind impacts, parking,

05:11:33.100 --> 05:11:36.279
stormwater runoff, compatibility with surrounding land uses,

05:11:37.034 --> 05:11:40.807
noise, trespassing, resident safety from stray golf

05:11:41.307 --> 05:11:45.062
balls, transition to the adjacent residential property, and building setbacks

05:11:45.126 --> 05:11:48.514
and step backs. All of which are land use

05:11:49.014 --> 05:11:52.609
planning considerations, and we thank staff for listening to us and considering the concerns

05:11:53.109 --> 05:11:56.831
as part of the preparation of their staff report. We have also had meetings

05:11:56.928 --> 05:12:01.151
with the applicants to convey our client's concerns over the original submission for

05:12:01.199 --> 05:12:04.924
a 10-story building with 153 units with

05:12:05.213 --> 05:12:08.248
reduced parking and rear and side yard setback

05:12:08.748 --> 05:12:12.358
reductions. Following the public meeting in April and comments received from

05:12:12.858 --> 05:12:16.437
staff, the— and the community, the applicant has revised their

05:12:16.937 --> 05:12:20.836
application to an 8-story building with 107

05:12:21.336 --> 05:12:26.907
17 units and approximately 433 bedrooms. I was happy to just hear Rachel

05:12:26.939 --> 05:12:30.710
say that she's supportive of staff's recommendation, which is

05:12:31.402 --> 05:12:33.770
for a maximum building height of 7 stories.

05:12:34.446 --> 05:12:37.757
This helps reduce the— reduce but not eliminate shadow

05:12:37.838 --> 05:12:40.577
and massing overlook concerns that were raised by my client,

05:12:41.790 --> 05:12:45.596
that a minimum rear yard setback of 7.5 be maintained

05:12:46.096 --> 05:12:49.372
was also a recommendation by staff, and this helps provide appropriate

05:12:49.872 --> 05:12:53.759
separation and transition, and it creates physical distance for safety,

05:12:54.354 --> 05:12:58.258
allows for landscaping, buffering, maintenance, privacy, and mitigation

05:12:58.290 --> 05:13:01.890
of activity, and reduces the potential for conflicts along the

05:13:02.390 --> 05:13:06.502
common property line with an active golf course. Another recommendation from staff

05:13:06.550 --> 05:13:09.426
was that no balconies be permitted along the rear facade,

05:13:10.005 --> 05:13:13.617
and we We just heard from Rachel that this helps address overlook

05:13:13.634 --> 05:13:16.989
and the compatibility issues. Also helps

05:13:17.489 --> 05:13:21.501
with noise and privacy and potential for conflicts by increasing separation

05:13:22.001 --> 05:13:25.467
between land uses. No common amenity areas are

05:13:25.596 --> 05:13:29.530
to be permitted along the rear and eastern lot line was another recommendation

05:13:30.030 --> 05:13:33.656
of staff. And this helps address compatibility between the residential use

05:13:34.090 --> 05:13:37.866
and the golf course activities, including concerns over noise, privacy,

05:13:37.980 --> 05:13:41.512
and potential conflicts. Staff also required an addition—

05:13:42.013 --> 05:13:45.296
an increase in parking from the 0.58 spaces

05:13:45.393 --> 05:13:49.242
per dwelling unit proposed by Rachel

05:13:49.742 --> 05:13:53.808
and her clients, and they recommended 0.92

05:13:54.308 --> 05:13:57.842
spaces per dwelling with a 15% commitment to required spaces for

05:13:58.342 --> 05:14:02.460
visitors. This helps address concerns regarding overflow of parking onto

05:14:02.960 --> 05:14:06.373
our client's lands and reduces the likelihood of trespassing onto

05:14:06.873 --> 05:14:10.702
our client's property in search of parking. Enhanced landscaping

05:14:11.202 --> 05:14:14.551
and fencing along the north and east property lines was also a recommendation of staff,

05:14:14.631 --> 05:14:18.014
and this helps with the trespassing concern as well as the concern

05:14:18.063 --> 05:14:22.071
over compatibility by providing screening and safety to the residents and

05:14:22.087 --> 05:14:25.503
protection of the golf course lands and provides for transition of the properties.

05:14:26.417 --> 05:14:30.685
And lastly, staff also recommended that a warning clause be put

05:14:31.185 --> 05:14:34.507
into and registered on title, warning of the golf course

05:14:35.007 --> 05:14:38.152
activities. And this helps advise residents

05:14:38.280 --> 05:14:40.753
of stray golf balls and helps address compatibility.

05:14:41.572 --> 05:14:45.506
Our clients are generally accepting of these recommendations made by staff

05:14:45.586 --> 05:14:49.102
as a compromise and respectfully request that council approve

05:14:49.311 --> 05:14:52.988
the, approve the staff report with the recommendations rather

05:14:53.488 --> 05:14:56.960
than the original or the revised application submitted by the applicant.

05:14:58.060 --> 05:15:02.896
Our clients continue to have some concerns over shadow and stormwater management impacts

05:15:02.993 --> 05:15:06.801
to the golf course. Adequate sunlight is very important for turf

05:15:06.817 --> 05:15:09.442
health and the maintenance of the golf course playing conditions.

05:15:11.433 --> 05:15:15.337
The reduction of the building height recommended by staff is therefore particularly important,

05:15:15.932 --> 05:15:20.318
and it has addressed that concern somewhat. Stormwater runoff onto neighboring

05:15:20.415 --> 05:15:24.221
golf of course, lands was also identified as a concern during the public process,

05:15:24.623 --> 05:15:28.329
and this has to be addressed during site plan approval. Our clients request

05:15:28.377 --> 05:15:31.874
that council and its decision ensures that these matters are,

05:15:32.147 --> 05:15:35.484
are addressed. Our clients, Cut and Fields, have participated in this process

05:15:35.597 --> 05:15:38.549
in good faith and recognize that these lands will likely be redeveloped.

05:15:39.062 --> 05:15:42.319
Their objective is not to prevent the redevelopment, but rather to ensure that this is

05:15:42.415 --> 05:15:48.015
ultimately constructed, represents good planning, not only for the applicant

05:15:48.515 --> 05:15:49.810
and the future residents of the proposed building, but also for the established properties that

05:15:49.842 --> 05:15:53.131
will live in this decision for decades. We therefore respectfully

05:15:53.147 --> 05:15:56.763
ask council to approve staff's report with the recommendations as submitted.

05:15:59.990 --> 05:16:03.719
Your microphone got cut off on the words thank you. Thank you. But we

05:16:04.219 --> 05:16:07.255
still heard you. Okay. All right, well, thank you very much. And is there any

05:16:07.755 --> 05:16:10.392
follow-up questions for the delegation? Councilor Chu.

05:16:11.700 --> 05:16:14.734
Thank you. Through you, I'm just very curious,

05:16:14.782 --> 05:16:18.217
just for my own clarity, are you satisfied with the reduced

05:16:18.717 --> 05:16:23.098
