05:16:23.756 --> 05:16:27.914
I am satisfied with that, with the recommendations

05:16:27.930 --> 05:16:32.971
that staff have put forward. My clients may have other aspirations,

05:16:33.003 --> 05:16:35.748
but definitely I am satisfied with those recommendations.

05:16:35.957 --> 05:16:39.653
Sorry, just that the one that the applicant applicant has put forward, you're okay

05:16:40.153 --> 05:16:43.983
with that? Pardon? The, the, the recommendations of

05:16:44.000 --> 05:16:47.284
staff with 7 stories, not the, not the proposals

05:16:47.380 --> 05:16:51.111
that the applicant has put forward at 8 stories, or that one, the original

05:16:51.611 --> 05:16:55.153
one at 10. We would not be satisfied with those. Okay, thank you. You're welcome.

05:16:56.689 --> 05:17:00.297
Thank you. I don't see anything more, so thank you very much.

05:17:00.379 --> 05:17:01.707
Appreciate your, your work there.

05:17:04.538 --> 05:17:07.279
And, uh, is Virgilio Villa here?

05:17:09.634 --> 05:17:11.698
Come on forward. Thank you for waiting, we appreciate it.

05:17:13.583 --> 05:17:16.635
Also from the Cutten, uh, Cutten Club, so Cutten Fields.

05:17:16.684 --> 05:17:17.626
So thank you very much.

05:17:20.657 --> 05:17:24.385
May I start? Thank you, Mayor Guthrie, members of council,

05:17:24.417 --> 05:17:28.418
and city staff. Good evening, my name is Virgilio Villa, chief operating

05:17:28.467 --> 05:17:31.972
officer of Cutten Fields. With me tonight to answer questions,

05:17:32.357 --> 05:17:36.268
if I may call up at some time, is William Griem, our golf course superintendent.

05:17:37.230 --> 05:17:40.837
I would like to first thank the city staff for the considerable work

05:17:41.337 --> 05:17:44.428
that they've done to reviewing this application. Throughout this process, Cutton Fields

05:17:44.524 --> 05:17:47.650
has raised a number of concerns. Staff listened, engaged with

05:17:48.150 --> 05:17:51.642
us, and addressed several, several key items to this with the recommendations

05:17:51.738 --> 05:17:55.169
for before council. The reduction in height, greater separation

05:17:55.265 --> 05:17:58.777
of our from property, restrictions on balconies, rear yard amenity space,

05:17:59.309 --> 05:18:02.986
and higher parking requirements are meaningful improvements. We sincerely

05:18:03.018 --> 05:18:06.548
appreciate your work. I also want to be very clear

05:18:07.048 --> 05:18:10.517
about our position. Cutton Fields is not opposed to development. We're not opposed to student

05:18:10.550 --> 05:18:13.971
housing. We understand the need for housing and the importance of the

05:18:14.295 --> 05:18:17.713
University of Guelph, and we support the continued growth of our city.

05:18:18.410 --> 05:18:21.768
Our concern is this particular development.

05:18:21.998 --> 05:18:24.834
Inuit, at its scale and its location.

05:18:25.571 --> 05:18:29.016
For cotton fields, responsible development begins with compatible land

05:18:29.516 --> 05:18:33.055
use. Guelph has identified strategic growth areas where high

05:18:33.103 --> 05:18:36.468
density— higher density compact development intended

05:18:36.968 --> 05:18:40.458
to be concentrated. Guelph's planning approach also speaks to

05:18:40.474 --> 05:18:43.935
creating complete communities that meet

05:18:44.435 --> 05:18:47.829
the long-term needs of the people who live in them. We support that vision.

05:18:48.423 --> 05:18:52.478
But responsible growth is not simply about how much housing

05:18:52.494 --> 05:18:56.310
we build. It is also about where we build it, its scale,

05:18:56.422 --> 05:19:00.526
and how it fits in the community already surrounding it. Cuddenfields is

05:19:01.026 --> 05:19:05.143
not a recreational amenity available to residents of this development, as stated

05:19:05.175 --> 05:19:09.311
in Attachment 8. We are an active private golf course, tennis facility,

05:19:09.407 --> 05:19:13.271
and community institution that has been part of Guelph for

05:19:13.592 --> 05:19:16.845
for generations. There are still concerns remaining.

05:19:17.213 --> 05:19:21.219
Our 9th hole still sits immediately beside the development. Sunlight does

05:19:21.719 --> 05:19:25.065
affect turf health, moisture, growing conditions,

05:19:25.530 --> 05:19:29.664
disease pressure, and our ability to sustainably maintain

05:19:29.680 --> 05:19:33.606
the golf course. We appreciate staff's recommendation and reduction in height,

05:19:33.943 --> 05:19:37.677
but once the building is constructed and these environmental challenges change,

05:19:38.013 --> 05:19:41.719
we cannot relocate the 9th hole. This is also an

05:19:42.219 --> 05:19:46.537
issue of safety and separation. There is an active golf course. Balls— golf

05:19:47.037 --> 05:19:50.584
balls do wander off, uh, without intention. Appropriate setbacks,

05:19:50.713 --> 05:19:53.973
fencing, landscaping, and buffering protect cotton fields,

05:19:54.487 --> 05:19:58.438
but just as important, they protect the future residents of

05:19:58.938 --> 05:20:02.212
this development. We cannot predict what will happen in the future,

05:20:02.758 --> 05:20:06.018
nor is this our true argument. Our concern is

05:20:06.130 --> 05:20:09.624
that And when potential conflicts between two different land uses

05:20:10.217 --> 05:20:13.679
can reasonably be identified today, this is the time to

05:20:14.179 --> 05:20:17.348
address them, not after they occur. Members of council,

05:20:17.413 --> 05:20:19.960
housing matters, student housing matters,

05:20:20.618 --> 05:20:24.031
growth matters. We are— but where

05:20:24.223 --> 05:20:28.165
that growth occurs, its scale and how it interacts

05:20:28.229 --> 05:20:31.290
with established neighboring uses matter as well.

05:20:31.707 --> 05:20:35.640
If council approves this application, please hold every line staff

05:20:35.688 --> 05:20:39.333
have drawn to 7 stories, the setback

05:20:39.557 --> 05:20:43.058
staff has declined to reduce, the parking

05:20:43.154 --> 05:20:46.542
rates of 0.92 spaces per— excuse

05:20:47.042 --> 05:20:50.283
me, per unit. These protections matter because

05:20:51.038 --> 05:20:55.020
what we see as being proposed as student housing and then

05:20:55.052 --> 05:20:58.745
addressed as apartment units where it can't

05:20:59.245 --> 05:21:02.149
be answered. What is it? Is it apartment units or student housing?

05:21:02.679 --> 05:21:06.292
The high density still remains with the, the fact

05:21:06.792 --> 05:21:10.113
that it is going to be student housing. If approval is

05:21:10.225 --> 05:21:13.292
given tonight, we respectfully ask that they remain intact.

05:21:13.758 --> 05:21:17.531
These are protection matters that the staff have been reviewed in this

05:21:18.031 --> 05:21:21.321
application, responding concerns through, uh, raised through this process.

05:21:21.931 --> 05:21:25.479
City staff have moved this proposal considerably from where it

05:21:25.979 --> 05:21:30.505
began, and we thank them for that. Our position is not that nothing

05:21:30.617 --> 05:21:34.230
to be built there. Our position is what is built

05:21:34.551 --> 05:21:38.549
must have the best opportunity to coexist successfully with the established

05:21:39.049 --> 05:21:42.066
community and the neighboring uses. For Cotton Field,

05:21:42.483 --> 05:21:45.149
that is responsible development.

05:21:49.082 --> 05:21:52.999
We support growth, we do. We support housing, we do.

05:21:53.496 --> 05:21:57.589
We support student housing. We're simply asking for the right development

05:21:57.669 --> 05:21:59.964
at the right scale in the right location.

05:22:00.719 --> 05:22:04.185
For this, I thank you for your time and consideration. Great,

05:22:04.234 --> 05:22:07.123
thank you very much. And any follow-up questions at this time?

05:22:08.439 --> 05:22:11.568
Downer and then Busutil, please. Thank you. Through you, Mr.

05:22:11.617 --> 05:22:15.693
Mayor, so I just want to— so you're of the same

05:22:16.193 --> 05:22:19.385
position as, um, the previous delegation

05:22:19.497 --> 05:22:22.675
that— yeah, the planner that, that was

05:22:23.028 --> 05:22:26.270
here just now before you, that if,

05:22:26.559 --> 05:22:29.929
if this is approved, that we stick to

05:22:30.429 --> 05:22:34.070
it? Like, you're— it, it's acceptable as long as

05:22:34.664 --> 05:22:37.874
we hit the planning staff's recommendations?

05:22:38.580 --> 05:22:41.887
It's not— not— it's not ideal. It's not what you would ideally. No, it's certainly

05:22:42.387 --> 05:22:45.598
not. Yeah, it— if, if anything, if you're going to pass this this

05:22:45.662 --> 05:22:49.099
evening, that is a recommendation in respect to take into

05:22:49.599 --> 05:22:53.099
account the recommendation of the staff. It's a protection mechanism in which

05:22:53.276 --> 05:22:56.665
we know that at least there is restrictions to how much and

05:22:57.165 --> 05:23:00.713
how high they can develop. Um, our biggest concern

05:23:00.825 --> 05:23:03.620
is, is it the right development?

05:23:03.829 --> 05:23:06.510
Is it the right scale? And is it in the right position.

05:23:06.943 --> 05:23:10.213
The high density really is going to be obstructed to our,

05:23:10.550 --> 05:23:14.077
our golf course. The scale of the actual development

05:23:14.577 --> 05:23:18.084
is going to be— not the lack of the word— and I'll

05:23:18.584 --> 05:23:21.723
be truthful, it's an eyesore. And, you know, we're,

05:23:22.397 --> 05:23:28.264
we're, we're in a position where we actually have establishments

05:23:28.328 --> 05:23:32.175
where, you know, it's a golf course, it's a recreational facility,

05:23:32.255 --> 05:23:34.741
but those who actually are part of Cottonfields.

05:23:35.419 --> 05:23:39.358
You know, people join us because of the sightlines in which they

05:23:39.858 --> 05:23:43.425
cherish. In respect to Mr.

05:23:43.570 --> 05:23:48.026
John Christensen, you know, the idea that he's

05:23:48.526 --> 05:23:51.817
going to be sandwiched between this big development and our

05:23:52.317 --> 05:23:56.500
golf course, it makes absolutely no sense where

05:23:56.725 --> 05:24:00.120
the total scale of this development really does affect the,

05:24:00.136 --> 05:24:03.969
you know, how it actually is in relation

05:24:04.081 --> 05:24:06.819
to who we are, to who Mr.

05:24:07.254 --> 05:24:10.505
Doran-Christiansen is and where they live. That's the principal home.

05:24:11.427 --> 05:24:14.662
It just does not make sense. We're not saying in any way

05:24:14.743 --> 05:24:18.572
or shape or form that we are against development. We are

05:24:18.620 --> 05:24:21.945
not against development at any, in any course. We know

05:24:22.445 --> 05:24:25.158
it needs to be developed. It should be developed, but when it's developed,

05:24:25.625 --> 05:24:28.686
but at what scale, you know, and what purpose.

05:24:29.475 --> 05:24:33.490
And is the purpose that's being proposed, is that the correct position,

05:24:33.523 --> 05:24:36.305
or is that the correct, uh, property to be, uh,

05:24:36.597 --> 05:24:40.059
developed for? Okay, thank you.

05:24:40.787 --> 05:24:42.418
Uh, and, and Councilor Buceto.

05:24:45.160 --> 05:24:48.773
Thank you. And through the mayor, thank you for your delegation. I just

