05:42:18.195 --> 05:42:21.566
then why the H? Right, so again, the,

05:42:21.710 --> 05:42:25.514
the city zoning bylaw requires municipal services to be adequate and available,

05:42:25.578 --> 05:42:29.590
and that's the test for city staff from the engineering department when zoning

05:42:29.670 --> 05:42:32.767
applications are put in front of council. And so that's roads,

05:42:32.799 --> 05:42:35.863
that's sewers, that's pipes, that's stormwater management.

05:42:35.927 --> 05:42:39.473
And so staff are looking at those reports at the zoning level to

05:42:39.973 --> 05:42:43.275
ensure that the site is viable for the zoning that is being requested.

05:42:44.269 --> 05:42:46.997
If an applicant gets the zoning and comes back in in the future at site

05:42:47.497 --> 05:42:50.655
plan with, you know, revisions to their design, a change in the concept, a changed

05:42:50.751 --> 05:42:54.377
